<asp:Content ID="Content2" ContentPlaceHolderID="ContentPlaceHolder1" Runat="Server">

    <div class="container">

                <div class="row">
            <div class="col-md-12">

                <div style="width:100%;height:110px;background-color:black;margin-top:25px;margin-bottom:25px;text-align:center;">
                    <h1 style="color:#ff5500;padding:25px;">Excercise </h1>
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>


        <div class="row">

            <div class="col-md-12">
                <span style="color:orange;font-size:25px;">what is exercise:</span>
                <p>
                    In kickboxing, exercise refers to the physical activity of practicing kickboxing techniques and movements. Kickboxing is a high-intensity workout that can help improve cardiovascular health, strength, and endurance .
                </p>

                <p>
                     Kickboxing exercises typically involve a combination of punches, kicks, knee strikes, and elbow strikes. These exercises can be performed on a heavy bag, focus mitts, or with a partner .
                </p>
                <p>
                    In addition to the physical benefits, kickboxing can also help improve mental health by reducing stress and anxiety .
                </p>

                <hr style="background-color:white;width:95%;margin-right:auto;margin-left:auto;" />

                <table class="table-active">

                    <tr>
                        <td style="font-size:21px;text-align:center;"> 
                            the principles of exercise in general, here are some tips to keep in mind before and after exercising:
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td style="color:orange;font-size:23px;">Before Exercise:</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <ul style="font-size:21px;padding:25px;">
                                <li>
                                    <span style="color:orangered;">Warm up:</span> It’s important to warm up your muscles before exercising to prevent injury. You can do this by stretching, jogging in place, or doing some light cardio.
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                   <span style="color:orangered;">Stay hydrated:</span>   Drink plenty of water before and during exercise to stay hydrated.
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <span style="color:orangered;">Wear appropriate clothing:</span>  Wear comfortable clothing and shoes that are appropriate for the type of exercise you’ll be doing.
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                  <span style="color:orangered;">Set realistic goals:</span>  Set goals that are challenging but achievable.
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td style="color:orange;font-size:23px;">After Exercise:</td>
                    </tr>
                                      <tr>
                        <td>
                            <ul style="font-size:21px;padding:25px;">
                                <li>
                                    <span style="color:orangered;">Cool down:</span> After exercising, it’s important to cool down your muscles to prevent injury. You can do this by stretching or doing some light cardio
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                   <span style="color:orangered;">Stretch:</span> Stretching after exercise can help improve flexibility and prevent muscle soreness.
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <span style="color:orangered;">Stay hydrated:</span> Continue to drink water after exercise to stay hydrated.
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                  <span style="color:orangered;">Rest:</span> Give your body time to rest and recover after exercising.
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                </table>

            </div>

            <div class="col-md-12">

                <table class="table-active" >

                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <td><h1 style="color:orange;">warm-up</h1></td>
                            <td><img src="Exercises/E19.png" width="230" height="230" /></td>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>

                    <tr>
                        <td colspan="2">
                            <p>
                                warm-up is a set of exercises that are performed before the main workout to prepare the body for the physical demands of the training session. A proper warm-up can help prevent injury and improve performance by increasing blood flow to the muscles, raising body temperature, and improving flexibility .
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                A typical warm-up in kickboxing might include some light cardio exercises such as jumping jacks or jogging in place, followed by some dynamic stretching exercises such as leg swings or arm circles. The warm-up should be performed for at least 5-10 minutes before moving on to more intense exercises .
                            </p>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td style="text-align:center"><img src="Exercises/E9.png" width="230" height="230" /></td>
                        <td style="text-align:center"><img src="Exercises/E10.png" width="230" height="230" /></td>
                    </tr>
                                  <tr>
                        <td style="text-align:center"> <img src="Exercises/E11.png" width="230" height="230" /></td>
                        <td style="text-align:center"><img src="Exercises/E13.png" width="230" height="230" /></td>
                    </tr>
                </table>

            </div>


             <div class="col-md-12">

                <table class="table-active" >

                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <td><h1 style="color:orange;">staying hydrated</h1></td>
                            <td style="text-align:right;"><img src="images/hydration.jpeg" width="350" height="300" style="border-radius:50%;" /></td>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>

                    <tr>
                        <td colspan="2">
                            <p>
staying hydrated is important to maintain optimal performance and prevent dehydration. During a workout, you lose fluids through sweating, and it’s important to replace these fluids by drinking water or other hydrating fluids.                            </p>
                            <p>
It’s recommended to drink water before, during, and after your kickboxing workout. The amount of water you need to drink depends on several factors such as your body weight, the intensity of your workout, and the temperature and humidity of your environment.                            </p>

                            <p>
                                A good rule of thumb is to drink at least 8 ounces of water every 15-20 minutes during your workout. If you’re working out for longer than an hour, you may want to consider a sports drink that contains electrolytes to help replace lost minerals.
                            </p>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
       
                </table>

            </div>


            <div class="col-md-12">

                <table class="table-active" >

     <tr>
         <td><h1 style="color:orange;">Wear appropriate clothing</h1></td>
     </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td colspan="2">
                            <p>
 it’s important to wear appropriate clothing that is comfortable and allows for a full range of motion. Here are some tips for choosing the right clothing for kickboxing:                            <p>
     </p>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
       <tr>
           <td>
               <ul style="font-size:21px;padding:25px;">
                   <li><span style="color:orangered;">Shoes:</span> Wear shoes that are lightweight and provide good support. Cross-training shoes or boxing shoes are a good choice.</li>
                   <li><span style="color:orangered;">Pants:</span> Wear pants that are comfortable and allow for a full range of motion. Sweatpants or shorts are a good choice.</li>
                   <li><span style="color:orangered;">Shirt:</span>Wear a shirt that is lightweight and breathable. A moisture-wicking shirt can help keep you cool and dry during your workout. </li>
                   <li><span style="color:orangered;">Hand wraps:</span>If you’re planning to do bag work or sparring, you may want to wear hand wraps to protect your hands. </li>
                   <li><span style="color:orangered;">Gloves:</span> If you’re planning to do bag work or sparring, you’ll need a pair of gloves. Choose gloves that fit well and provide good support.</li>
               </ul>
           </td>
       </tr>
                </table>

            </div>


              <div class="col-md-12">

                <table class="table-active" >

     <tr>
         <td><h1 style="color:orange;">setting realistic goals</h1></td>
     </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td colspan="2">
                            <p>
setting realistic goals is important to help you stay motivated and track your progress. Here are some tips for setting realistic goal     </p>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
       <tr>
           <td>
               <ul style="font-size:21px;padding:25px;">
                   <li><span style="color:orangered;">Be specific:</span>Set specific goals that are measurable and achievable. For example, instead of saying “I want to get better at kickboxing,” set a goal like “I want to improve my roundhouse kick.”</li>
                   <li><span style="color:orangered;">Be realistic:</span>Set goals that are challenging but achievable. Don’t set goals that are too easy or too difficult</li>
                   <li><span style="color:orangered;">Set short-term and long-term goals:</span>Set both short-term and long-term goals. Short-term goals can help you stay motivated and track your progress, while long-term goals can help you stay focused on the big picture</li>
                   <li><span style="color:orangered;">Write down your goals:</span>Write down your goals and keep them somewhere visible. This can help you stay motivated and focused</li>
                   <li><span style="color:orangered;">Track your progress:</span>Keep track of your progress towards your goals. This can help you stay motivated and make adjustments as needed</li>
               </ul>
           </td>
       </tr>
                </table>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>

